Use a Map ordered from least to most recently used. Delete and reinsert accessed or replaced entries to refresh recency; evict the first entry when capacity is exceeded.

```javascript
function solve(capacity, operations) {
  const cache = new Map();
  const results = [];

  for (const [type, key, value] of operations) {
    if (type === "get") {
      if (!cache.has(key)) {
        results.push(-1);
      } else {
        const cachedValue = cache.get(key);
        results.push(cachedValue);
        cache.delete(key);
        cache.set(key, cachedValue);
      }
    } else if (type === "put") {
      cache.delete(key);
      cache.set(key, value);

      if (cache.size > capacity) {
        const oldestKey = cache.keys().next().value;
        cache.delete(oldestKey);
      }
    }
  }

  return results;
}
```

Call `solve(capacity, operations)` directly with `capacity > 0`. For n operations and g gets, time is O(n) assuming average O(1) Map operations; auxiliary space is O(min(n, capacity)), plus O(g) for the returned results.

